// Regex extraction and pure path helpers.
//
// `regex.extract(pattern, text)` is the native named-capture helper: a match
// returns a record whose labels are the capture names. Failure cases live in
// the pathological tree; this model example stays on the happy path. The
// `path` module is pure string manipulation, not filesystem I/O: `join`,
// `basename`, and `extension` compute over path-shaped strings and can be used
// in ordinary session mode.
def caps = regex.extract("^(?<stem>.*)\\.(?<ext>gandr)$", "examples/demo.gandr");

def joined = path.join("examples", "demo.gandr");

def leaf = path.basename(joined);

def suffix = path.extension(joined);

#{ capture = caps, leaf = leaf, path_ext = suffix }

// The harness checks:
//@ requires-feature: regex
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-def: caps
//@ expect-def: joined
//@ expect-last-value: #{capture = #{ext = "gandr", stem = "examples/demo"}, leaf = "demo.gandr", path_ext = "gandr"}
